--- Cross-rule fact provenance (DR-0045, the value-flow engine v1). A consumed
--- fact contributes its COMPUTED producer reach instead of only its declared
--- label: per producing rule, the rule's own non-fact sources join the whole
--- fact -- the opaque box that keeps implicit flows inside the reach -- and a
--- direct upstream fact binding contributes THAT fact's reach (the cross-rule
--- edge). Every unaccountable path -- table seed, workflow input, external
--- arrival, unattributable payload root -- contributes the LABEL TOKEN, which
--- stands for "the declared fact label applies" (Phase 0 semantics exactly).
---
--- Soundness shape, the field-signature discipline one hop further: the reach
--- never UNDER-reports. Own reads are in the whole fact; a direct fact root
--- contributes its producer's full reach; anything else degrades to the label
--- token. So a source truly reaching the fact's content is always in the
--- reach or absorbed by the token (coverage), while a fact whose real chain
--- is clean escapes an over-conservative label, bite -- the relief -- and an
--- untrusted chain through an UNLABELED fact finally injects as what it is:
--- bite on the integrity axis, the laundering closure.
---
--- The model is axis-neutral: `leak` stands for the denied confidentiality
--- flow or the denied integrity influence; `hot` marks a source the sink is
--- not cleared for on the axis under test.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-FACT-PROVENANCE is
  protecting BOOL .

  sorts Fact Tok TokList Cfg .
  subsort Tok < TokList .

  ops fA fB : -> Fact [ctor] .

  --- reach tokens: a HOT source the sink cannot take, a COLD one it can,
  --- the label token of fact F, and a direct upstream fact edge.
  op hot : -> Tok [ctor] .
  op cold : -> Tok [ctor] .
  op lbl : Fact -> Tok [ctor] .
  op edge : Fact -> Tok [ctor] .
  op nilT : -> TokList [ctor] .
  op _._ : Tok TokList -> TokList [ctor] .

  op none : -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op __ : Cfg Cfg -> Cfg [ctor assoc comm id: none] .

  --- ground truth per scenario: each fact's producer contributions (own reads
  --- + payload-root contributions, already flattened to tokens and edges),
  --- whether the sink is cleared for fact F's DECLARED label, and the egress
  --- of fact F's content to the sink under audit.
  op prod : Fact TokList -> Cfg [ctor] .     --- producer contributions of F
  op lblOk : Fact Bool -> Cfg [ctor] .       --- sink cleared for F's declared label?
  op consume : Fact -> Cfg [ctor] .          --- the audited egress of F's content
  op leak : -> Cfg [ctor] .
  eq leak leak = leak .

  var F : Fact .  var T : Tok .  var TL TL2 : TokList .  var C : Cfg .  var B : Bool .

  op prodOf : Cfg Fact -> TokList .
  eq prodOf((prod(F, TL) C), F) = TL .
  eq prodOf(C, F) = nilT [owise] .

  op lblOkOf : Cfg Fact -> Bool .
  eq lblOkOf((lblOk(F, B) C), F) = B .
  eq lblOkOf(C, F) = true [owise] .

  --- does consuming F's reach deny at the sink? One edge hop is expanded --
  --- fA -> fB suffices for the two-hop scenarios; deeper chains are the
  --- fixpoint's induction, pinned by the Rust engine tests.
  op tokDenies : Tok Cfg -> Bool .
  eq tokDenies(hot, C) = true .
  eq tokDenies(cold, C) = false .
  eq tokDenies(lbl(F), C) = not lblOkOf(C, F) .
  eq tokDenies(edge(F), C) = listDenies(prodOf(C, F), C) .

  op listDenies : TokList Cfg -> Bool .
  eq listDenies(nilT, C) = false .
  eq listDenies((T . TL), C) = tokDenies(T, C) or listDenies(TL, C) .

  --- The consumption denial: egressing F's content denies iff any token of
  --- F's computed reach denies at the sink. The condition reads the config
  --- relationally (prodOf/lblOkOf); an AC-extension sub-match that drops a
  --- table entry hits an owise default chosen PERMISSIVE (nilT / true), so a
  --- sub-match can only UNDER-fire -- Solution searches are satisfied by the
  --- full match and NoSolution searches cannot be spuriously broken (the
  --- field-signature model's convention).
  crl [deny] : consume(F) C => consume(F) C leak
    if listDenies(prodOf((consume(F) C), F), (consume(F) C)) = true .
endm
